  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="3.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVEg">IV Eg</ref> 3.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3.1" corresp="#wit-f">⁊ gewitnes sý geset to ælcere byrig ⁊ to ælcum hundrode:</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3.1" corresp="#wit-c">⁊ gehitnæs sý geset to ælcere byrig ⁊ to ælcum hundrode:</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3.1" corresp="#wit-q">Et in omni ciuitate fidele testimonium inueniatur, ut omnis rationis uia furandi intercludatur:</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="3.1" corresp="#wit-c">⁊ gewitnes sý geset to ælcere byrig ⁊ to ælcum hundrode:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-c">And a body of standing witnesses shall be appointed for every borough and for every hundred.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock">And witness is to be appointed for each borough and for each hundred.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und zu jeder Stadt und zu jeder Hundertschaft werde Zeugenschaft eingesetzt:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let a body of witnesses be appointed for every borough and for every hundred:</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="378"><label>comparable role (per Liebermann)</label> <ref target="clause:Hu_4">Hu 4</ref> <quote>IV Eg 3:1 – 6 envisages organized panels playing the role given by Hu. 4 to the head of the hundred</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="185"><ref target="clause:IIIAtr_3-1">III Atr 3.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">C's ‘gehitnæs’ should be corrected to ‘gewit-’.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#whitelock">id. omits the hundred</note>
      </div>
    </body>
